# Unit-test build for the AppState statusRead parse (E5 history-epochs invariant) + (CX-G-12, 13-04)
# the full app lifecycle, minimal TestEntryApp entry.
#   monkeyc -f test.jungle -o bin/faBolusGarmin-test.prg -y developer_key.der -d venu3s --unit-test -w
#   monkeydo bin/faBolusGarmin-test.prg venu3s -t
#
# NARROW-MAIN (2026-08-27): the paused direct-pump + direct-cgm BLE engines (and their oracle-parity/
# resume tests) are REMOVED from main and live on the dev/direct-ble + experimental branches only, so
# this jungle no longer compiles direct-pump/engine — just source/app + tests.
#
# The AppState parse tests (tests/HistoryEpochsTest.mc, tests/GlucosePlotBoundsTest.mc — Phase 09.13
# glucose plot height customization, D-05/D-06/D-07/D-08/D-10) need AppState.mc compiled in; VA-32 needs
# DetailsView.mc (tests/DetailsRowYTest.mc). These used to be cherry-picked (AppState.mc + RemoteComm.mc +
# BgComplication.mc + DetailsView.mc — AppState's only app-code deps, verified: every other capitalized ref
# in it is comment-only) specifically to AVOID EatingRelay.mc and its private EatingSense barrel.
#
# CX-G-12 (13-04): that exclusion left the HIGH/CRIT poll-liveness (C5-01/CX-G-05, FaBolusApp.pollTick +
# HeartRateRelay.emitIfDue) and dedup-reset (CX-G-07, FaBolusApp.notifyNewAlerts) mechanisms completely
# outside the test binary — see the old headers on PollBackoffTest.mc/OutcomeWatchdogTest.mc/
# HoldTeardownTest.mc ("the FaBolusApp poll that drives them isn't test-compiled — see test.jungle").
# FaBolusApp.mc's dependency graph (onStart/getInitialView/notifyNewAlerts → Nav → the full screen carousel
# → every View/Delegate in source/app) can't be cherry-picked without re-deriving the same closure
# monkey.jungle already declares, so base.sourcePath now takes source/app WHOLESALE (mirroring
# monkey.jungle/official.jungle) instead of an enumerated file list, and base.resourcePath is added to
# resolve the Rez.Drawables/Rez.Strings references those Views pull in. base.barrelPath is declared so
# EatingRelay.mc's `using EatingSenseKit;` resolves.
#
# This makes the test binary barrel-gated + Sensor/Background-permission-gated exactly like the two
# shipping jungles: a machine without barrels/EatingSense.barrel (the private faBolusNudge SDK output)
# can no longer build test.jungle either. That is an accepted, deliberate trade-off — CX-G-12 requires the
# real shipping lifecycle code (not a subset) in the test binary — not a regression to fix here; see
# 13-04-SUMMARY.md. excludeAnnotations still drops BgComplication's no-op stub so only the real
# (:complications) publisher compiles on venu3s.
# G-L4 (19-03): pin the same explicit type check level as monkey.jungle/official.jungle — see
# monkey.jungle's comment for why Level 2 (Informative), not Level 3 (Strict): the test binary compiles
# the WHOLE app + the full test suite, and several pre-existing test files use PolyType/Any patterns
# that only Level 3 flags — out of this plan's scope.
project.typecheck = 2
project.manifest = manifest-test.xml
base.sourcePath = source/app;tests
base.resourcePath = resources;resources-complications
base.barrelPath = barrels/EatingSense.barrel
base.excludeAnnotations = nocomplications
